From: KlaussCPU Linux port
Subject: [PATCH] Add the KlaussCPU port

src/klausscpu: ffi_call, variadic calls and closures for the KlaussCPU C
ABI (klausscpu-llvm ABI.md, version 3: LP64, soft float, R0-R3 then
8-byte stack slots, aggregates up to 16 bytes in one or two words and
returned in R12/R11, larger ones by reference and through sret in R0,
a 32-byte home area in variadic calls).  _Complex types are supported
(aggregates); Go closures and static trampolines are not.  Closures
use dynamic trampolines in libffi's W+X pages; the I-cache snoops the
core's own stores, so no cache maintenance is needed (or available to
user code).  configure.host and Makefile.am name the port; Buildroot
autoreconfs libffi (LIBFFI_AUTORECONF = YES).

--- a/configure.host	2025-02-08 18:30:36.000000000 +0200
+++ b/configure.host	2026-11-11 20:44:59.685380389 +0200
@@ -136,6 +136,11 @@
